description:
Objective: under the PROTECTED runtime profile, the JetBrains agent launcher marks the session for the wrappers, so CQ-R13c2's wrappers can refuse to fall back when a protected runtime path vanishes. This is CQ-R01's follow-up 6, 'Wrapper-side fallbacks under strong', from the architect note on CQ-R13. The human placed it among the certification-gating items in the architect REPL on 2026-10-30.

Split out of CQ-R13 (task-f4811a72) by architect-e4b7eee0 on 2026-10-30. It is file-disjoint from CQ-R13c2. The contract shared with CQ-R13c2 is the env var MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED, whose value is exactly '1'.

Deliverable:
- In moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/util/TerminalAgentLauncher.kt, selectProtectedAgentRuntime adds MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1 to the env it returns, beside MOE_DAEMON_PATH and MOE_PROXY_PATH. It appears only in ProtectedAgentRuntime.Selected.
- The legacy path (protectedAgentRuntime returning null) and resolveAgentEnvOverrides stay unchanged and never set it.
- Tests in moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/util/TerminalAgentLauncherTest.kt:
  - Selected carries exactly those three variables;
  - the legacy path adds none of them;
  - a Refused selection carries nothing.

Out of scope:
- the wrappers (CQ-R13c2);
- the other R01 follow-ups, now in the CQ-RF protected runtime follow-ups epic;
- VS Code;
- .moe edits.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): cmd.exe /d /c "cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --rerun". This is cd moe-jetbrains && ./gradlew test. The WSL host has no Linux JDK, so Gradle runs through Windows cmd.exe, as CQ-R01's verification did.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- TerminalAgentLauncher.kt:
  - selectProtectedAgentRuntime (~78-100) builds a linkedMapOf env with MOE_DAEMON_PATH and MOE_PROXY_PATH from RuntimeSelectionPolicy.installedArtifact;
  - protectedAgentRuntime (~103-110) returns null under legacy;
  - resolveContext (~215-261) uses `selected?.env ?: resolveAgentEnvOverrides(script.source)`.
- The WSL bash command maps every override value through toWslPath (~434), which returns non-drive values unchanged. PowerShell renders `$env:` assignments (~484).
- CQ-R01's protected-selection tests are L1-L3 in RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt and use exact map equality. The rendering tests are in TerminalAgentLauncherTest.kt (buildWslBashCommandForTest ~251).
